# CV bullet points

<!-- Generated by scripts/build_docs.py from results/**/*.json. Every number traces to results/. -->

- Built a tested Python experimentation toolkit (SRM checks, CUPED, Lan-DeMets sequential boundaries, IPW/AIPW, clustered DiD, T/X-learner uplift) and validated the estimators against reference implementations and Monte Carlo simulations with known effects. For example, sequential boundaries held the false-positive rate at {{ nul.obrien_fleming.rejection_rate | pct(1) }}, against {{ nul.naive_peeking.rejection_rate | pct(1) }} for naive peeking across 10 looks.
- Re-audited an observational mobile-vs-desktop conversion analysis on {{ "{:,}".format(ga.all_sessions.n_sessions) }} Google Analytics sessions. Added visitor-clustered SEs and propensity adjustment on session-start covariates only, and found that a suspected internal-traffic segment ({{ ga.internal_traffic.share_of_desktop_conversions | pct(0) }} of desktop conversions) roughly halved the adjusted gap ({{ gA.estimate | pp(2) }} to {{ gX.estimate | pp(2) }}). Recommended a randomized test sized by power analysis instead of a redesign launch.
- Built an uplift-targeting policy on {{ "{:,}".format(crit.n_rows) }} Criteo users with honest train/validation/test splits. Targeting the top {{ cb.decision.chosen_depth | pct(0) }} earned {{ (cb.decision.test_profit_per_user * 1000) | money }} per 1,000 held-out users against {{ (cb.decision.test_random_profit_per_user * 1000) | money }} for random targeting under stated cost assumptions. Packaged as a CLI report and Streamlit app that refuse to interpret results when trust checks fail.
